I haven't seen a reply to the second part of this so here goes:
<Spoiler Ahead>




















By wielding the worm tooth and reading the enchant weapon scroll, 
you turn it into a crysknife.  I've read fortune cookies saying
something about not unwielding the crysknife until you've used it,
but I don't recall having any particular problem.  As I recall from
Dune, crysknifes did have to draw blood before they could be 
sheathed(sp?).

Personally, I've always thought crysknives should be more
effective than they actually seem to be in hack.  Granted 
they are only knives, so they shouldn't be as effective as a 
sword, but you'd think they be as good as Sting.

They are much harder to get the Sting (IMHO).  I guess they aren't
really artifacts, because there were many crysknives, but only one
Sting.

...Wait a sec...

I just checked the spoiler file, and it show them as having a +3
hit modifier (the highest of any weapon).  Not sure why I didn't
think they worked too well.  Maybe it was just my perception, or
possibly the old version of hack I was playing on.

Looking at the damage, they do 1-10 damage against both large and
small monsters.  This is not as good as a typical sword against
big monsters, but better than many swords against small monsters.
Makes sense.  I guess it's effectiveness is about right.  (Looking
down the small monster damage list, it looks like only thing MUCH
better than a crysknife are bows.  I don't use the spoilers much
so I never knew this.  Bows are pretty lame against big monster 
though).



Wait, I remember now!  In some old version of hack, you could only
enchant it to +1, because the enchant weapon scroll didin't work on
them in the usual way.  I hope that's been fixed.
